---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const nav = [
  { id:'privacy', label:'Privacy Policy' },
  { id:'terms', label:'Terms & Conditions' },
  { id:'returns', label:'Returns Policy' },
  { id:'acceptable-use', label:'Acceptable Use' },
  { id:'cookie', label:'Cookie Policy' },
  { id:'dmca', label:'DMCA' },
  { id:'disclaimer', label:'Disclaimer' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Policies" description="Ballmecca's privacy policy, terms, and legal information." path="/policies">
  <section class="container" style="padding:48px 0;">
    <h1 class="display" style="font-size:44px;">Our policies.</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">View all our policies below. Questions? <a href="mailto:support@ballmecca.com">support@ballmecca.com</a></p>
    <div class="pol-grid">
      <aside class="pol-nav" aria-label="Policy sections">
        <ul>{nav.map((n) => <li><a href={`#${n.id}`}>{n.label}</a></li>)}</ul>
      </aside>
      <div class="pol-body">

        <section id="privacy">
          <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-muted last-updated">Last updated: July 2, 2026</p>
          <p>This privacy notice for Ballmecca Inc. ("Company," "we," "us," or "our"), describes how and why we might collect, store, use, and/or share ("process") your information when you use our services ("Services"), such as when you:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Download and use our mobile application (Ballmecca), or any other application of ours that links to this privacy notice</li>
            <li>Engage with us in other related ways, including any sales, marketing, or events</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Questions or concerns?</strong> Reading this privacy notice will help you understand your privacy rights and choices. If you do not agree with our policies and practices, please do not use our Services. If you still have any questions or concerns, please contact us at support@ballmecca.com.</p>

          <h3>1. WHAT INFORMATION DO WE COLLECT?</h3>
          <p><strong>Personal information you disclose to us</strong></p>
          <p>We collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us when you register on the Services, express an interest in obtaining information about us or our products and Services, when you participate in activities on the Services, or otherwise when you contact us.</p>
          <p>The personal information we collect may include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Names, phone numbers, and email addresses</li>
            <li>Usernames, passwords, and billing address</li>
            <li>Contact and authentication data</li>
            <li>Birthdate, gender, height, zip code, and sport(s)</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Payment Data:</strong> Athlete payments are processed by Stripe, Inc.; we do not store your full card number. Coach subscriptions are billed through the Apple App Store or Google Play. Coaches who receive payouts provide tax and identity information (such as a Social Security or Taxpayer Identification Number) <strong>directly to Stripe</strong> for payouts and tax reporting — Ballmecca does not collect or store it.</p>
          <p><strong>Application Data:</strong> If you use our application(s), we may collect geolocation information, mobile device access data, push notifications, and other device information necessary to maintain security and operation of our application(s).</p>

          <h3>2. HOW DO WE PROCESS YOUR INFORMATION?</h3>
          <p>We process your personal information for a variety of reasons, including:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>To facilitate account creation and authentication</li>
            <li>To deliver and facilitate delivery of services to the user</li>
            <li>To respond to user inquiries and provide support</li>
            <li>To send administrative information</li>
            <li>To fulfill and manage your orders</li>
            <li>To enable user-to-user communications</li>
            <li>To request feedback and contact you about your use of our Services</li>
            <li>To send marketing and promotional communications</li>
            <li>To protect our Services from fraud and security threats</li>
            <li>To identify usage trends and improve our Services</li>
            <li>To deliver personalized content and advertising</li>
            <li>To deliver relevant training content and connect you with coaches</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>3. WHO DO WE SHARE YOUR INFORMATION WITH?</h3>
          <p>We share information with service providers ("subprocessors") that process it on our behalf, and in a few specific situations. We do not sell your personal information for money. Key subprocessors include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Google / Firebase</strong> — app hosting, database, storage, authentication, and website hosting</li>
            <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — athlete payment processing and coach payouts (Stripe Connect)</li>
            <li><strong>Apple &amp; Google Play</strong> — billing for coach subscriptions purchased in-app</li>
            <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — website usage analytics</li>
            <li><strong>Meta (Facebook)</strong> — advertising measurement and attribution (see Section 6 regarding "sharing")</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We may also share information: with <strong>other users</strong> as needed to provide the coaching you request (for example, delivering your video to your chosen coach); in a <strong>business transfer</strong> (merger, acquisition, or sale of assets); and to <strong>comply with law</strong> or protect rights, safety, and the integrity of the Services.</p>

          <h3>4. HOW DO WE KEEP YOUR INFORMATION SAFE?</h3>
          <p>We have implemented appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational security measures designed to protect the security of any personal information we process. However, no electronic transmission over the Internet can be guaranteed to be 100% secure. We cannot promise that hackers or unauthorized third parties will not be able to defeat our security.</p>

          <h3>5. WHAT ARE YOUR PRIVACY RIGHTS?</h3>
          <p>Depending on where you are located, you may have certain rights regarding your personal information, including:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The right to request access to your personal information</li>
            <li>The right to request correction or deletion of your personal information</li>
            <li>The right to restrict the processing of your personal information</li>
            <li>The right to withdraw consent at any time</li>
            <li>The right to opt out of marketing communications</li>
          </ul>
          <p>You can make such requests by contacting us at support@ballmecca.com.</p>

          <h3>6. CALIFORNIA RESIDENTS — SPECIFIC PRIVACY RIGHTS</h3>
          <p>If you are a California resident, you have additional rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA), including the right to know what personal information is collected, used, or shared; the right to delete or correct personal information; and the right to opt out of the "sale" or "sharing" of personal information.</p>
          <p>We use analytics and advertising partners — including Google Analytics and Meta (Facebook) — whose technologies may constitute "sharing" of personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising under the CCPA/CPRA. <strong>You have the right to opt out of this sharing.</strong> To opt out today, email <a href="mailto:support@ballmecca.com">support@ballmecca.com</a>; we are also adding a self-serve "Your Privacy Choices" control to this website. We do not knowingly sell or share the personal information of anyone we know to be under 16.</p>

          <h3>7. OTHER U.S. STATE PRIVACY RIGHTS</h3>
          <p>Residents of Virginia, Colorado, Connecticut, Utah, Texas, Oregon, Montana, and other states with comprehensive privacy laws may have rights to access, correct, delete, and obtain a copy of their personal data, and to opt out of targeted advertising, the sale of personal data, and certain profiling. To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:support@ballmecca.com">support@ballmecca.com</a>; you may also appeal a decision by replying to our response. We do not use your personal information for decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects without human involvement.</p>

          <h3>8. HOW LONG DO WE KEEP YOUR INFORMATION?</h3>
          <p>We keep your information only as long as necessary for the purposes in this notice, unless a longer period is required by law. As a general guide: account and profile data is kept while your account is active and for a reasonable period after closure; uploaded video is kept for the period needed to deliver and support your coaching and then deleted or anonymized; and payment and tax records are kept as required by law (typically several years). When we no longer have a legitimate need, we delete or anonymize the information.</p>

          <h3>9. DO WE MAKE UPDATES TO THIS NOTICE?</h3>
          <p>Yes, we will update this notice as necessary to stay compliant with relevant laws. The updated version will be indicated by an updated "Last updated" date. We encourage you to review this privacy notice periodically.</p>

          <h3>10. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY</h3>
          <p>Ballmecca serves athletes of many ages, including children under 13 — but a child under 13 may use the Services <strong>only through a parent-managed account</strong>. We require that a parent or legal guardian create and control the account, consent to our collection of the child's information (including any performance video the child uploads), and supervise the child's use.</p>
          <p>Consistent with the U.S. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA): we seek a parent's consent before a child's personal information is collected; we limit what we collect from a child to what is needed to provide the coaching; we do not condition a child's participation on disclosing more than is reasonably necessary; and <strong>we do not knowingly permit behavioral or targeted advertising to children under 13</strong>.</p>
          <p>A parent or guardian may review the personal information we have collected from their child, ask us to delete it, or refuse further collection by contacting <a href="mailto:support@ballmecca.com">support@ballmecca.com</a>. If you believe a child has provided personal information without the required parental involvement, contact us and we will take appropriate steps to delete it.</p>

          <h3>11. EUROPEAN UNION, EEA, AND UNITED KINGDOM</h3>
          <p>Ballmecca is based in the United States and primarily serves U.S. users; we do not actively target the EU, EEA, or UK. If you access the Services from those regions, the following applies. Our legal bases for processing are: performance of a contract (to provide the Services), your consent (for example, analytics and advertising cookies, and marketing), our legitimate interests (to operate, secure, and improve the Services), and compliance with legal obligations. You have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict, or port your data, to object to processing, to withdraw consent, and to lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority. Because we operate from the United States, using the Services involves transferring your information to the U.S.; where required, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as the Standard Contractual Clauses. To exercise any right, email <a href="mailto:support@ballmecca.com">support@ballmecca.com</a>.</p>

          <h3>12. HOW CAN YOU CONTACT US?</h3>
          <p>If you have questions about this notice or wish to exercise a privacy right, email support@ballmecca.com. <strong>We aim to respond to privacy requests within 30 days.</strong> You may also reach us by post at:</p>
          <p>
            Ballmecca Inc.<br />
            74 East Glenwood Avenue #8116<br />
            Smyrna, DE 19977<br />
            United States
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="terms">
          <h2>Terms & Conditions</h2>
          <p class="text-muted last-updated">Last updated: July 2, 2026</p>

          <h3>1. AGREEMENT TO TERMS</h3>
          <p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") are a legally binding agreement between you and Ballmecca Inc. ("Ballmecca," "we," "us," or "our"), governing your access to and use of the https://ballmecca.com website, the Ballmecca mobile application, and any related media and services (collectively, the "Services"). We are located at 74 East Glenwood Avenue #8116, Smyrna, DE 19977.</p>
          <p>By creating an account or using the Services, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and by our <a href="#privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="#acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>, and <a href="#returns">Returns Policy</a>, each incorporated by reference. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE, DO NOT USE THE SERVICES.</p>
          <p>We may update these Terms from time to time by updating the "Last updated" date; material changes may also be communicated through the Services. Your continued use after changes take effect constitutes acceptance.</p>

          <h3>2. THE SERVICES — A MARKETPLACE OF INDEPENDENT COACHES</h3>
          <p>Ballmecca is a marketplace that connects athletes (and their parents) with independent sports coaches for video-based coaching, coach demonstrations, and general guidance. <strong>Coaches are independent third parties, not employees, agents, or representatives of Ballmecca.</strong> We do not employ, supervise, direct, or control coaches, and we do not guarantee the quality, suitability, safety, legality, or outcome of any coaching or any coach's conduct.</p>
          <p>We review the credentials a coach submits before allowing them to coach on the Services. <strong>This credential review is not a background check, an identity guarantee, or an assurance of safety</strong>, and it does not make Ballmecca responsible for a coach's acts or omissions. You are responsible for your own decisions about whom to engage, and — for a minor athlete — a parent or guardian is responsible for supervising that engagement.</p>

          <h3>3. ELIGIBILITY AND ACCOUNTS</h3>
          <p>To use the Services you must be able to form a binding contract. Account types include <strong>Athlete</strong>, <strong>Parent-managed athlete</strong>, <strong>Coach</strong>, <strong>College-athlete coach</strong>, and <strong>Recruiter</strong>.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Children under 13.</strong> A child under 13 may use the Services only through a <strong>parent-managed account</strong> created and controlled by a parent or legal guardian who provides consent as described in our <a href="#privacy">Privacy Policy</a> (Children's Privacy). The parent or guardian is the account holder, is responsible for all activity on the account, and enters into these Terms on the child's behalf.</li>
            <li><strong>Minors 13–17.</strong> A minor who is at least 13 may use the Services only with the involvement and permission of a parent or legal guardian, who agrees to these Terms on the minor's behalf and is responsible for the minor's use.</li>
            <li>You agree to provide accurate information, keep it current, keep your credentials secure, and are responsible for all activity under your account.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>4. PAYMENTS, FEES, AND PAYOUTS</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Athlete payments.</strong> Athletes pay for coaching sessions through our payment processor, <strong>Stripe</strong>. Each coach sets the price of their session, and <strong>Ballmecca adds a 15% platform fee on top of the coach's price</strong>. The total (session price + platform fee, plus any applicable taxes) is shown before you pay and is charged when you book.</li>
            <li><strong>Coach subscriptions.</strong> Optional coach subscription plans are sold as <strong>auto-renewing in-app purchases through the Apple App Store or Google Play</strong>. Payment is charged to your store account at confirmation, and <strong>the subscription renews automatically for the same period until you cancel</strong>. You can manage or cancel in your App Store or Google Play account settings; cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period. Apple or Google — not Ballmecca — process these charges and any related refunds.</li>
            <li><strong>Coach payouts.</strong> Coaches receive payouts through <strong>Stripe Connect</strong> and provide the tax and identity information Stripe requires directly to Stripe. Coaches are solely responsible for their own taxes and for the accuracy of their payout information. We may withhold or reverse payouts in cases of fraud, chargebacks, refunds, or violations of these Terms.</li>
            <li><strong>Taxes.</strong> Prices may be exclusive of taxes, which may be added where required.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Refunds are governed by our <a href="#returns">Returns Policy</a>.</p>

          <h3>5. REFERRALS AND THE COACHING FUND</h3>
          <p>We may offer referral rewards (for example, a discount for athletes, or a share of Ballmecca's fee for coaches whose referred athletes purchase sessions) and a Coaching Fund that helps sponsor free sessions for eligible athletes. Rewards and credits <strong>have no cash value, are non-transferable, and are non-refundable</strong>. We may change, limit, or discontinue any referral program or the Coaching Fund, and may revoke rewards obtained through fraud, abuse, or violation of these Terms.</p>

          <h3>6. COACH TERMS AND CODE OF CONDUCT</h3>
          <p>If you use the Services as a coach, you additionally represent, warrant, and agree that:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>You are an <strong>independent contractor</strong>, not an employee or agent of Ballmecca, and nothing here creates a partnership, joint venture, or employment relationship;</li>
            <li>Any credentials, certifications, or experience you provide are <strong>truthful and accurate</strong>, and you are legally permitted to provide coaching;</li>
            <li>You will comply with all applicable laws, including those relating to working with minors and any mandatory-reporting obligations that apply to you;</li>
            <li>When coaching minors, you will <strong>keep communication and coaching on the Services</strong>, will not solicit or arrange off-platform or in-person contact, and will not request or share private contact information; and</li>
            <li>You will not engage in harassment, discrimination, sexual content, or any conduct that endangers an athlete. Violations may result in immediate removal.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>7. RECRUITER TERMS</h3>
          <p>Recruiter features are provided for lawful talent-evaluation purposes only. If you use the Services as a recruiter, you agree that you will <strong>not</strong> scrape, harvest, resell, or redistribute athlete data; will <strong>not</strong> contact minor athletes off-platform or without appropriate parental involvement; will comply with all applicable recruiting rules and laws; and will use information accessed through the Services only for legitimate evaluation — not to harass, unlawfully profile, or discriminate.</p>

          <h3>8. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS</h3>
          <p>The Services and their contents — all software, text, graphics, designs, audio, video, and our trademarks, service marks, and logos (collectively, the "Content" and "Marks") — are owned by or licensed to Ballmecca and protected by intellectual-property laws. Except as expressly permitted, you may not copy, reproduce, republish, distribute, sell, license, or exploit the Content or Marks without our prior written permission. This does not affect your ownership of your own Contributions (Section 12).</p>

          <h3>9. USER REPRESENTATIONS</h3>
          <p>By using the Services, you represent and warrant that: you have the legal capacity to agree to these Terms (or a parent/guardian has agreed on your behalf); you meet the eligibility requirements in Section 3; you will not access the Services through automated or non-human means except as expressly permitted; and you will not use the Services for any illegal or unauthorized purpose or in violation of any law.</p>

          <h3>10. PROHIBITED ACTIVITIES</h3>
          <p>You agree not to misuse the Services. Prohibited activities are described in our <a href="#acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a> and include, without limitation: harvesting data or content without permission; defrauding or misleading us or other users; circumventing security or fees; harassing, abusing, or harming another person; impersonation; uploading malware; and any activity that violates applicable law or endangers a minor.</p>

          <h3>11. USER CONTRIBUTIONS</h3>
          <p>The Services allow you to submit content and materials, including performance videos ("Contributions"). By submitting Contributions, you represent and warrant that: you own or have the necessary rights and permissions to them; you have consent from any identifiable individuals (and, for any minor shown, from that minor's parent or guardian); they are accurate and not misleading; they are not spam, obscene, unlawful, or infringing; and they do not violate anyone's privacy or publicity rights.</p>

          <h3>12. CONTRIBUTION LICENSE</h3>
          <p>When you submit Contributions (including performance videos), you grant Ballmecca a non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide license to host, store, process, display, and transmit those Contributions <strong>solely to operate and provide the Services</strong> — for example, delivering your video to the coach you selected and returning that coach's feedback to you. This license lasts only as long as needed to provide the Services and to comply with law; it ends when you delete the Contribution or close your account, except for residual backup copies or where retention is required by law.</p>
          <p>We will <strong>not</strong> use your Contributions for marketing, advertising, or promotional purposes without your separate, opt-in consent. For any athlete under 18, such use additionally requires the verifiable consent of the athlete's parent or guardian. You retain ownership of your Contributions. We may remove or restrict Contributions that violate these Terms or our Acceptable Use Policy.</p>

          <h3>13. GUIDELINES FOR REVIEWS</h3>
          <p>If you post a review, you must have firsthand experience with the person or service reviewed; must not include profanity, abusive or discriminatory language, or references to illegal activity; must not post false or misleading statements; and must not organize campaigns to post reviews. We may accept, reject, or remove reviews in our discretion and are not responsible for any review's content.</p>

          <h3>14. APPLE AND GOOGLE APP STORES</h3>
          <p>If you obtain the Ballmecca application through the Apple App Store or Google Play, you also agree to that store's applicable terms, and the following apply: these Terms are between you and Ballmecca, not with Apple or Google; the store provider has no obligation to furnish maintenance or support; to the maximum extent permitted by law, the store provider has no warranty obligation and is not responsible for product or intellectual-property claims or the application's legal/regulatory compliance; and <strong>Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them</strong>. You represent that you are not located in an embargoed country or on a prohibited-party list, and you will comply with applicable third-party usage rules.</p>

          <h3>15. SERVICES MANAGEMENT</h3>
          <p>We may, but are not obligated to: monitor the Services for violations; take appropriate action against anyone who violates these Terms or the law; refuse, restrict, or remove content or access; and otherwise manage the Services to protect our rights, protect the safety of users, and keep the Services functioning.</p>

          <h3>16. TERM AND TERMINATION</h3>
          <p>These Terms remain in effect while you use the Services. We may suspend or terminate your access at any time, with or without notice, for any reason, including violation of these Terms. If we terminate your account, you may not register a new one without our permission. Provisions that by their nature should survive termination will survive.</p>

          <h3>17. MODIFICATIONS AND INTERRUPTIONS</h3>
          <p>We may change, modify, suspend, or discontinue all or part of the Services at any time. We are not liable for any such change, suspension, or discontinuance, or for any unavailability of the Services.</p>

          <h3>18. GOVERNING LAW</h3>
          <p>These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Delaware, without regard to its conflict-of-law principles.</p>

          <h3>19. DISPUTE RESOLUTION; ARBITRATION; CLASS-ACTION WAIVER</h3>
          <p><strong>Please read this section carefully — it affects your legal rights.</strong></p>
          <p><strong>Informal resolution.</strong> Before starting arbitration, you agree to first contact us at support@ballmecca.com and try to resolve the dispute informally for at least thirty (30) days.</p>
          <p><strong>Binding arbitration.</strong> Except for the exceptions below, any dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or the Services will be resolved by <strong>final and binding arbitration</strong> administered by the American Arbitration Association (AAA) under its <strong>Consumer Arbitration Rules</strong>, before a single arbitrator, seated in Delaware (or by video/telephone where available). Judgment on the award may be entered in any court of competent jurisdiction.</p>
          <p><strong>Class-action and jury waiver.</strong> Disputes will be arbitrated <strong>only on an individual basis</strong>. You and Ballmecca waive any right to a jury trial and waive any right to bring or participate in a class, collective, or representative action.</p>
          <p><strong>Exceptions.</strong> Either party may bring a claim in small-claims court, and either party may seek injunctive or equitable relief for intellectual-property or unauthorized-use claims in court.</p>
          <p><strong>Your right to opt out.</strong> You may opt out of this arbitration agreement within <strong>30 days</strong> of first accepting these Terms by emailing support@ballmecca.com with your name and a statement that you opt out of arbitration. Opting out will not affect any other part of these Terms.</p>
          <p>Where a user is a minor, a parent or guardian agrees to this section on the minor's behalf. Some provisions may not be enforceable in all jurisdictions or as to all users; if any part is held unenforceable, the remainder continues to apply.</p>

          <h3>20. ASSUMPTION OF RISK</h3>
          <p>Sports, training, and physical activity carry inherent risks of injury. The Services provide informational coaching only and are not medical, health, or fitness advice. You are responsible for exercising safely and within your ability, and for consulting a healthcare provider before beginning any new activity. <strong>By using the Services, you (and, for a minor, the parent or guardian) knowingly assume the risks of participating in athletic activity</strong>, and agree that, to the fullest extent permitted by law, Ballmecca and its coaches are not liable for resulting injuries. See also our <a href="#disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.</p>

          <h3>21. DISCLAIMER</h3>
          <p>THE SERVICES ARE PROVIDED ON AN "AS-IS" AND "AS-AVAILABLE" BASIS, AND YOUR USE IS AT YOUR SOLE RISK. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE DISCLAIM ALL WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE MAKE NO WARRANTY THAT THE SERVICES WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, SECURE, OR ERROR-FREE, OR ABOUT THE CONDUCT OF ANY COACH, ATHLETE, OR OTHER USER.</p>

          <h3>22. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY</h3>
          <p>TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, IN NO EVENT WILL BALLMECCA OR ITS DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, OR AGENTS BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES. OUR TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM WILL BE LIMITED TO THE LESSER OF THE AMOUNT YOU PAID TO BALLMECCA DURING THE SIX (6) MONTHS BEFORE THE EVENT GIVING RISE TO THE CLAIM, OR $200.00 USD. SOME JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW CERTAIN LIMITATIONS, SO SOME OF THE ABOVE MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU.</p>

          <h3>23. INDEMNIFICATION</h3>
          <p>You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold Ballmecca harmless from any loss, liability, claim, or demand, including reasonable legal fees, arising from: your Contributions; your use of the Services; your breach of these Terms or your representations; your violation of any law or third-party right; or any harmful act toward another user.</p>

          <h3>24. CONTACT US</h3>
          <p>For questions or complaints, contact us at:</p>
          <p>
            Ballmecca Inc.<br />
            74 East Glenwood Avenue #8116<br />
            Smyrna, DE 19977<br />
            United States<br />
            support@ballmecca.com
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="returns">
          <h2>Returns Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-muted last-updated">Last updated: July 2, 2026</p>

          <h3>Coaching sessions</h3>
          <p>Coaching sessions are personalized services delivered by independent coaches, so once a session has been delivered it is generally non-refundable. That said, we want every session to be worthwhile: if you are not satisfied, contact <a href="mailto:support@ballmecca.com">support@ballmecca.com</a> within <strong>7 days</strong> of receiving your feedback and we will work with you to make it right — which may include a credit or, at our discretion, a refund. Contacting us within the 7-day window does not guarantee a refund; each request is reviewed on its specific facts.</p>

          <h3>Coach subscriptions</h3>
          <p>Coach subscriptions are billed through the Apple App Store or Google Play and are governed by those stores' billing and refund policies. You can manage or cancel a subscription in your App Store or Google Play account settings, and any refund requests for those charges are handled by Apple or Google.</p>

          <h3>Credits</h3>
          <p>Referral discounts and Coaching Fund credits have no cash value and are non-refundable.</p>

          <h3>Questions</h3>
          <p>If you have any questions concerning our return policy, please contact us at: support@ballmecca.com</p>
        </section>

        <section id="acceptable-use">
          <h2>Acceptable Use Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-muted last-updated">Last updated: July 3, 2026</p>
          <p>This Acceptable Use Policy is part of our <a href="#terms">Terms of Service</a> and applies to everyone who uses Ballmecca. Because our community includes young athletes, keeping the Services safe is a priority. Your continued use means you accept this Policy.</p>

          <h3>Prohibited conduct</h3>
          <p>When using the Services, you must comply with all applicable laws and this Policy. You may not:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Harass, bully, threaten, defame, or discriminate against any person</li>
            <li>Post or share obscene, sexual, violent, hateful, or otherwise objectionable content</li>
            <li>Share another person's private or personal information without permission, or record or share images of others without their consent</li>
            <li>Impersonate any person or misrepresent your identity, credentials, or affiliation</li>
            <li>Defraud or mislead us or other users, or circumvent fees or transact off-platform to avoid them</li>
            <li>Systematically harvest data or content, or collect usernames or email addresses for unsolicited messages</li>
            <li>Circumvent, disable, or interfere with security features, or upload malware or otherwise disrupt the Services</li>
            <li>Use the Services for any unlawful purpose or to infringe others' intellectual-property rights (see our <a href="#dmca">DMCA</a> policy)</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Protecting minors — zero tolerance</h3>
          <p>We have <strong>zero tolerance</strong> for the sexual exploitation of, or any harm to, children. You must never:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Produce, share, request, or solicit child sexual abuse material (CSAM) or any sexual content involving a minor;</li>
            <li>Groom, sexually solicit, or attempt to develop an inappropriate relationship with a minor;</li>
